# l7a (earthai-l7a) crontab lines for the page-vector service (#6821, scripts/workers/vector-search). INSTALLED 2026-10-17 (phase 4, #6843) in root's
# crontab on l7a, beside the existing lines (backup first: crontab -l > /root/backups/crontab-<date>).
#
# Every 30 min: apply page_translations rows updated since the checkpoint (vectors in RAM, text in
# text/pages.sqlite; no index save), then a heartbeat that stamps last_delta_at.
# Every 2 h at :45, --reconcile: one ~1 min scan of every served page_id, adding what the service lacks and
# removing what Supabase no longer serves. NOT optional: updated_at is the Mongo source time, so most
# newly embedded rows are behind the checkpoint and only this pass finds them (4,055 of 4,736 in the
# first 26 h; sync-delta.mjs header, step 4).
# Each reconcile also compares the text store's fingerprints with Supabase's (byte lengths; header-only, so
# no slower), and replaces stale text (in-place edits leave updated_at alone; sync-delta.mjs step 5).
# 03:40 UTC: delta + reconcile --hash (md5 of one seventh of the translations, the weekday's: every row weekly;
# it catches a same-length edit), then save a new generation (tmp + rename) and compare the row count with
# Supabase (exit 4 and a COUNT DRIFT line when the drift is above 0.1%).
# The reconcile lines cap the heap at 2 GB: uncapped, the client-side diff peaked at 2.35 GB RSS (mostly GC
# slack) against 1.27 GB capped at 1.5 GB, same wall time (2026-10-17).
# All three share one flock (text-fingerprints.mjs, run once by hand, takes it too), so the nightly save never overlaps a delta and no two deltas run at once; the
# half-hourly one skips (-n) when the lock is held, the nightly one waits up to 15 min for it.
# :10 and :40: freshness-check.mjs — ntfy sourcelibrary-uptime once per state change when the service is
# down, the last delta is older than 2 h, the last reconcile older than 6 h, or the row count drifts more
# than 0.5% from the reconcile's Supabase count. It reads no database.
*/30 * * * * flock -n /tmp/vector-search-delta.lock systemd-run --quiet --scope --slice=sourcelibrary.slice /usr/bin/node --no-warnings --env-file=/root/sourcelibrary/.env.production.local /data/vector-search/app/sync-delta.mjs >> /data/vector-search/logs/delta.log 2>&1
45 */2 * * * flock -w 600 /tmp/vector-search-delta.lock systemd-run --quiet --scope --slice=sourcelibrary.slice /usr/bin/node --no-warnings --max-old-space-size=2048 --env-file=/root/sourcelibrary/.env.production.local /data/vector-search/app/sync-delta.mjs --reconcile >> /data/vector-search/logs/delta.log 2>&1
40 3 * * * flock -w 900 /tmp/vector-search-delta.lock systemd-run --quiet --scope --slice=sourcelibrary.slice /usr/bin/node --no-warnings --max-old-space-size=2048 --env-file=/root/sourcelibrary/.env.production.local /data/vector-search/app/sync-delta.mjs --reconcile --hash --save --count-check >> /data/vector-search/logs/delta.log 2>&1
10,40 * * * * flock -n /tmp/vector-search-freshness.lock systemd-run --quiet --scope --slice=sourcelibrary.slice /usr/bin/node --no-warnings --env-file=/root/sourcelibrary/.env.production.local /data/vector-search/app/freshness-check.mjs >> /data/vector-search/logs/freshness.log 2>&1

# Mondays 06:00 UTC: the Librarian page-link gauge (#6946, scripts/audit/librarian-citation-gauge.ts). INSTALLED
# 2026-10-18 in root's crontab on l7a (backup: /root/backups/crontab-20261018-215139). Samples 20 readers' first turns of
# the last 7 days, Opus judges (claude -p, subscription; at most 25 calls, no Gemini) label every page link; one JSON line
# to /var/log/sourcelibrary/librarian-quality.jsonl and a row in librarian-quality.md beside it. ntfy sourcelibrary-uptime
# and a #6946 comment only when the wrong-page rate moves 10 points above (or back under) its trailing 4-run median.
# Guarded on the file so it waits for the merge; flock -n so two never overlap; timeout 2h.
0 6 * * 1 f=/data/scratch/sl/sourcelibrary/scripts/audit/librarian-citation-gauge.ts; [ -f $f ] && cd /data/scratch/sl/sourcelibrary && flock -n /tmp/librarian-citation-gauge.lock timeout 2h systemd-run --quiet --scope --slice=sourcelibrary.slice /usr/bin/npx tsx --env-file=/root/sourcelibrary/.env.production.local $f >> /data/scratch/sl/logs/librarian-citation-gauge.log 2>&1  # weekly page-link gauge, #6946

# Every 10 min: the Librarian citation fixer, DRY-RUN (#6946 stage 1, scripts/workers/librarian-citation-fixer.ts). INSTALLED
# 2026-10-20 in root's crontab on l7a (backup: /root/backups/crontab-20261020-005126). New AI turns from embassy_messages → Claude Sonnet
# (claude -p, subscription; no Gemini) → proposed page-link edits in librarian_citation_fixes, one document per answer. Writes
# NOTHING else: not embassy_messages, not the threads, not the replay cache. Nothing reads librarian_citation_fixes yet.
# At most 8 calls a run and 200 answers a day; skips the run when this box's Claude account is at >= 80% of its 5-hour
# window or >= 90% of its week. Guarded on the file so it waits for the merge; flock -n so two never overlap; timeout 30m.
*/10 * * * * f=/data/scratch/sl/sourcelibrary/scripts/workers/librarian-citation-fixer.ts; [ -f $f ] && cd /data/scratch/sl/sourcelibrary && flock -n /tmp/librarian-citation-fixer.lock timeout 30m systemd-run --quiet --scope --slice=sourcelibrary.slice /usr/bin/npx tsx --env-file=/root/sourcelibrary/.env.production.local $f >> /data/scratch/sl/logs/librarian-citation-fixer.log 2>&1  # citation fixer DRY-RUN, #6946

# Refused pages (#7170): every 3 h at :20, read up to 80 pages Gemini refused (RECITATION / three-strike fail stamps) in
# visible or held books, with the next reader the refused-pages row of scripts/lib/ocr-routing-table.json names (Sonnet or
# Opus through claude -p on this box's subscription; a page the first reader fails goes to Opus), write them through
# cli-ocr.mjs apply, then translate them with Opus (cli-translate.mjs apply) where the book already has translations.
# No Gemini, no paid API. Skips the run when this box's Claude account is at >= 70% of its week. Backlog at install:
# 4,568 pages in visible or held books (2026-10-23). Output per day under /data/scratch/sl/refused-pages/, resumable.
# PATH carries /root/.local/bin, where claude lives on l7a: cron's bare PATH does not, and claude-ocr.mjs calls `claude`.
20 */3 * * * export PATH=/root/.local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin; f=/data/scratch/sl/sourcelibrary/scripts/batch/refused-pages.mjs; [ -f $f ] && cd /data/scratch/sl/sourcelibrary && flock -n /tmp/refused-pages.lock timeout 2h systemd-run --quiet --scope --slice=sourcelibrary.slice /usr/bin/node --no-warnings --env-file=/root/sourcelibrary/.env.production.local $f run --out=/data/scratch/sl/refused-pages/$(date +\%F) --max-pages=80 --apply >> /data/scratch/sl/logs/refused-pages.log 2>&1  # #7170
